From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] settings: gather our settings under System > Yacer

Move every setting this build adds into one category below CoreELEC's,
in the order they matter most to whoever opens it:

- Video: HDR10+ to Dolby Vision (20_01), from System > CoreELEC
- Audio: the audio lead (11_10) and dialogue normalisation defeat (20_02),
  from System > CoreELEC, whose Passthrough Audio group was ours and goes
  with them
- AI: the provider, its address, key and model, and the test (07_02,
  07_07), from Player > Subtitles
- Subtitles: Brightness (05_02), AI translate subtitles
  (07_02), Repair and its options (07_01) with AI repair (07_03), and
  Realign (07_04), from Player > Subtitles

Dialogue normalisation defeat now applies to AC-3 / E-AC-3 only by default;
TrueHD Atmos and DTS can still be ticked.

The setting ids are unchanged, so saved values carry over, and settings left
behind still depend on them by id. Kodi's and CoreELEC's menus are back to
their own settings.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
